# Security headers for the Netlify-hosted site.
#
# The CSP enforces only the directives that are worth enforcing and safe to enforce here.
#
# script-src is deliberately ABSENT. A URL-allowlist script-src cannot be made correct on this
# site: header bidding picks bidder scripts at auction time from a long and changing tail of
# domains, so any list is stale within weeks. It would also not be worth having if it were
# correct, because the policy needs 'unsafe-inline' for the ad and analytics tags, and that
# alone lets an injected inline script run. OWASP and Google both say allowlist policies are
# ineffective against XSS for exactly this reason; the effective form is a per-request nonce
# with 'strict-dynamic'. That is a real piece of work (a nonce on every inline script, and
# CDN-cached HTML reuses its nonce) and it would still trust everything prebid loads, so it
# does not address third-party ad JS either. Output escaping is what actually holds this line:
# see composables/useLinkify.js, which escapes before it linkifies.
#
# It was previously report-only with an allowlist, reporting to Sentry. That produced ~14,500
# violation events a day, all of them script-src-elem from ad domains, with no action attached
# to any of them, and no protection either, since report-only blocks nothing.
#
# What IS enforced below was measured, not guessed: 24 hours of report-only data contained
# violations of script-src-elem ONLY. Nothing tripped object-src, frame-ancestors or worker-src,
# so enforcing those three changes no behaviour. base-uri was not in the old policy at all and
# is the one real gap it had: without it an injected <base> tag reroutes every relative script
# URL on the page. worker-src gains 'self' because the site registers a PWA service worker from
# its own origin, which a bare "worker-src blob:" would have blocked the moment it was enforced.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'self'; worker-src 'self' blob:
